1
00:01:32,650 --> 00:01:34,990
[Forging Justice]

2
00:01:35,240 --> 00:01:37,690
[Episode 3]

3
00:01:38,509 --> 00:01:39,070
Later,

4
00:01:39,870 --> 00:01:40,950
ask Zheng to take you guys

5
00:01:40,950 --> 00:01:42,750
to look around the street market

6
00:01:43,789 --> 00:01:45,650
and to conduct an investigation.

7
00:01:47,640 --> 00:01:50,070
Liu Erlin said
he mistook the person for someone else.

8
00:01:50,070 --> 00:01:51,560
Then he and his defense lawyer

9
00:01:51,560 --> 00:01:52,350
should figure out a way

10
00:01:52,350 --> 00:01:53,310
to prove it.

11
00:01:54,280 --> 00:01:54,789
Why should we

12
00:01:54,789 --> 00:01:55,789
help him prove it?

13
00:01:58,479 --> 00:02:00,760
That's not under the jurisdiction
of our court, is it?

14
00:02:00,760 --> 00:02:02,040
Investigating evidence and finding clues

15
00:02:02,040 --> 00:02:03,950
are the jobs
of the police and the procuratorate.

16
00:02:03,950 --> 00:02:05,200
As long as we discover that

17
00:02:05,200 --> 00:02:06,040
there's insufficient evidence

18
00:02:06,040 --> 00:02:07,170
with unclear facts,

19
00:02:07,310 --> 00:02:09,430
we should either send it back
for supplementary investigation

20
00:02:09,430 --> 00:02:10,310
or just

21
00:02:10,750 --> 00:02:11,870
acquit the suspect.

22
00:02:11,870 --> 00:02:13,530
Why should we investigate it?

23
00:02:14,520 --> 00:02:15,050
Alright.

24
00:02:15,560 --> 00:02:16,690
Whether you go or not

25
00:02:16,870 --> 00:02:17,630
is up to you.

26
00:02:25,829 --> 00:02:31,860
[Nanyu County People's Court,
People's Procuratorate]

27
00:02:34,360 --> 00:02:35,160
Chen Yizhong!

28
00:02:45,190 --> 00:02:45,710
What does he mean?

29
00:02:45,710 --> 00:02:46,240
Let's go.

30
00:02:46,240 --> 00:02:47,300
Where are we going?

31
00:02:48,000 --> 00:02:49,400
-Let's go.
-I don't know.

32
00:02:51,079 --> 00:02:51,430
Um...

33
00:02:51,910 --> 00:02:52,970
Where are we going?

34
00:02:56,920 --> 00:03:00,930
[Nanyu County Legal Advisory Office]

35
00:02:58,750 --> 00:03:00,610
Comrade, here's a letter for you.

36
00:03:26,750 --> 00:03:27,329
Hello.

37
00:03:27,750 --> 00:03:28,540
Who are you looking for?

38
00:03:28,540 --> 00:03:31,150
We're students from the University
of Political Science and Law.

39
00:03:31,150 --> 00:03:33,950
We're having an internship
in Nanyu County Court.

40
00:03:34,150 --> 00:03:35,240
I remember you guys now.

41
00:03:35,240 --> 00:03:36,800
I saw you all in court yesterday.

42
00:03:36,800 --> 00:03:38,190
Come on. Have a seat.

43
00:03:39,560 --> 00:03:40,750
Since you're court interns,

44
00:03:40,750 --> 00:03:41,520
what are you

45
00:03:41,520 --> 00:03:42,180
doing here?

46
00:03:42,750 --> 00:03:43,710
We sat in on the trial

47
00:03:43,710 --> 00:03:45,190
of Liu Erlin's case yesterday.

48
00:03:45,190 --> 00:03:47,720
There are some questions
we'd like to ask you.

49
00:03:49,000 --> 00:03:51,000
We can't talk to you about this case.

50
00:03:51,120 --> 00:03:52,120
We're still busy.

51
00:03:57,280 --> 00:03:57,880
It's fine.

52
00:03:58,910 --> 00:04:00,180
As long as it's not against the rules,

53
00:04:00,180 --> 00:04:01,310
we can talk about it.

54
00:04:02,400 --> 00:04:03,080
Come on.

55
00:04:03,280 --> 00:04:03,940
Have a seat.

56
00:04:04,420 --> 00:04:05,360
No need. Don't bother.

57
00:04:05,360 --> 00:04:05,870
Have a seat.

58
00:04:05,870 --> 00:04:06,770
Let me get you some water.

59
00:04:06,770 --> 00:04:08,830
Actually, we have just one question.

60
00:04:08,870 --> 00:04:10,000
Do you think Liu Erlin

61
00:04:10,000 --> 00:04:11,580
was committing armed robbery,

62
00:04:11,580 --> 00:04:13,110
or as he said in his defense,

63
00:04:13,240 --> 00:04:14,300
he was just joking?

64
00:04:15,560 --> 00:04:16,360
We think?

65
00:04:16,870 --> 00:04:18,160
Does it matter what we think?

66
00:04:18,160 --> 00:04:19,360
Of course it matters.

67
00:04:19,459 --> 00:04:21,060
You are his defense lawyers.

68
00:04:25,600 --> 00:04:26,200
Of course.

69
00:04:26,480 --> 00:04:27,750
Liu Erlin's statement

70
00:04:27,950 --> 00:04:29,010
might also be true.

71
00:04:29,360 --> 00:04:30,480
Then why didn't you launch

72
00:04:30,480 --> 00:04:31,390
a factual defense,

73
00:04:31,390 --> 00:04:32,560
and why did you just say
he was a first-time

74
00:04:32,560 --> 00:04:33,240
and casual offender?

75
00:04:33,240 --> 00:04:33,920
In this way, weren't you admitting

76
00:04:33,920 --> 00:04:35,780
that he committed armed robbery?

77
00:04:36,070 --> 00:04:36,600
Li Xiang.

78
00:04:36,830 --> 00:04:37,430
Thank you.

79
00:04:37,680 --> 00:04:38,680
They have doubts.

80
00:04:38,920 --> 00:04:40,580
Help them clear up the doubts.

81
00:04:44,510 --> 00:04:45,510
Here's the thing.

82
00:04:45,950 --> 00:04:47,000
Mr. Wang here

83
00:04:47,120 --> 00:04:48,310
did that out of a desire to protect

84
00:04:48,310 --> 00:04:49,360
the defendant.

85
00:04:49,870 --> 00:04:51,360
If we plead not guilty,

86
00:04:52,159 --> 00:04:53,270
and the court rejects it,

87
00:04:53,270 --> 00:04:54,159
they might even say

88
00:04:54,159 --> 00:04:55,950
the defendant has a bad attitude
towards admitting his crime,

89
00:04:55,950 --> 00:04:58,880
which would be even worse
for the defendant instead.

90
00:05:03,560 --> 00:05:04,680
Do you guys think

91
00:05:04,680 --> 00:05:05,600
the question you asked

92
00:05:05,600 --> 00:05:06,880
is particularly sharp?

93
00:05:06,880 --> 00:05:08,000
Mr. Wang, we are students.

94
00:05:08,000 --> 00:05:08,870
We just want to discuss...

95
00:05:08,870 --> 00:05:10,400
So what if you're students?

96
00:05:10,510 --> 00:05:13,310
Does that mean you can talk big
without substance?

97
00:05:17,250 --> 00:05:17,880
Alright.

98
00:05:18,510 --> 00:05:19,430
We're going to have a meeting.

99
00:05:19,430 --> 00:05:21,030
We won't keep you any longer.

100
00:05:21,270 --> 00:05:22,040
We won't disturb you anymore.

101
00:05:22,040 --> 00:05:22,640
Thank you.

102
00:05:23,120 --> 00:05:23,920
It's alright.

103
00:05:23,920 --> 00:05:25,000
We are indeed busy.

104
00:05:26,750 --> 00:05:29,310
Are you from the People's University
of Political Science and Law?

105
00:05:29,310 --> 00:05:29,680
Yes.

106
00:05:30,190 --> 00:05:31,990
How was it? Did you get anything?

107
00:05:32,270 --> 00:05:33,330
Such institutions

108
00:05:33,360 --> 00:05:34,760
are like deaf men's ears.

109
00:05:35,000 --> 00:05:35,830
But at least deaf men's ears

110
00:05:35,830 --> 00:05:37,230
have aesthetic effects.

111
00:05:38,390 --> 00:05:39,630
It's not easy for them, either.

112
00:05:39,630 --> 00:05:41,600
They are caught between the procuratorate
and the court.

113
00:05:41,600 --> 00:05:42,240
According to what they said,

114
00:05:42,240 --> 00:05:43,510
if you defend the case,

115
00:05:43,600 --> 00:05:44,600
the sentencing will be enhanced instead.

116
00:05:44,600 --> 00:05:46,200
Isn't that an exaggeration?

117
00:05:46,240 --> 00:05:47,570
You'd better leave now.

118
00:05:59,240 --> 00:06:00,170
Going to college

119
00:06:01,120 --> 00:06:02,450
has made them all fools.

120
00:06:07,720 --> 00:06:09,650
Actually, the question they asked

121
00:06:11,040 --> 00:06:13,170
is what I've been thinking about, too.

122
00:06:14,630 --> 00:06:15,240
Li Xiang.

123
00:06:16,360 --> 00:06:18,290
What kind of situation is this now?

124
00:06:18,360 --> 00:06:19,600
They don't punish
the hardworking or the lazy ones.

125
00:06:19,600 --> 00:06:21,400
They only punish the blind ones.

126
00:06:21,720 --> 00:06:22,650
I'm warning you.

127
00:06:23,190 --> 00:06:25,270
Regarding the rape case
you're handling,

128
00:06:25,270 --> 00:06:26,920
you must defend the case according to

129
00:06:26,920 --> 00:06:28,580
the basic approach we've set.

130
00:06:28,920 --> 00:06:30,380
Don't stick your neck out.

131
00:06:30,600 --> 00:06:31,060
Well...

132
00:06:32,000 --> 00:06:33,240
Isn't this more obvious?

133
00:06:33,240 --> 00:06:34,920
It's adultery, not rape.

134
00:06:36,240 --> 00:06:37,560
If you say so,

135
00:06:38,159 --> 00:06:39,690
you can defend it yourself.

136
00:06:39,920 --> 00:06:41,630
You don't know what's good for you.

137
00:06:41,630 --> 00:06:42,430
That's perfect.

138
00:06:42,430 --> 00:06:43,890
If you don't want to defend the case,

139
00:06:43,890 --> 00:06:45,690
I can collaborate with Li Xiang.

140
00:06:47,510 --> 00:06:50,170
You're intervening in everything,
aren't you?

141
00:06:50,270 --> 00:06:51,730
I'll go get some hot water.

142
00:06:53,950 --> 00:06:54,390
Wang.

143
00:06:55,070 --> 00:06:56,470
Do you think this is okay?

144
00:06:57,750 --> 00:06:59,550
I'll go ask Director Hong again.

145
00:07:02,480 --> 00:07:03,340
Suit yourself.

146
00:07:09,000 --> 00:07:09,950
Exactly.

147
00:07:11,050 --> 00:07:12,870
I had thought that after being assigned
to the Justice Bureau,

148
00:07:12,870 --> 00:07:13,530
I would at least get to

149
00:07:13,530 --> 00:07:14,660
manage a few people.

150
00:07:14,920 --> 00:07:15,560
I didn't expect

151
00:07:15,560 --> 00:07:16,490
to be assigned to

152
00:07:16,630 --> 00:07:17,760
such a crappy place.

153
00:07:18,130 --> 00:07:18,590
Come...

154
00:07:18,690 --> 00:07:19,740
Come in.

155
00:07:19,950 --> 00:07:20,800
That's all for now.

156
00:07:20,800 --> 00:07:23,000
I'll call you back later. Someone's here.

157
00:07:23,000 --> 00:07:23,660
Have a seat.

158
00:07:24,240 --> 00:07:25,120
My dear comrade-in-arms.

159
00:07:25,120 --> 00:07:25,780
Have a seat.

160
00:07:28,310 --> 00:07:28,910
Director.

161
00:07:29,190 --> 00:07:30,190
I have a case

162
00:07:30,390 --> 00:07:32,110
that I'd like to consult you about.

163
00:07:32,110 --> 00:07:33,440
What case is it? Tell me.

164
00:07:33,920 --> 00:07:35,000
It's the case about a teacher

165
00:07:35,000 --> 00:07:38,000
named Qiao Zhiliang
from the County No. 1 High School.

166
00:07:39,480 --> 00:07:40,540
Oh, it's that case.

167
00:07:41,560 --> 00:07:42,750
He's a beast.

168
00:07:43,920 --> 00:07:45,240
He even laid his hands on

169
00:07:45,240 --> 00:07:46,270
his own niece.

170
00:07:47,360 --> 00:07:47,870
Didn't that girl

171
00:07:47,870 --> 00:07:49,130
commit suicide later?

172
00:07:50,000 --> 00:07:50,920
He should be executed.

173
00:07:50,920 --> 00:07:52,580
He surely should be executed.

174
00:07:53,000 --> 00:07:53,390
Well,

175
00:07:53,750 --> 00:07:54,350
Director,

176
00:07:54,870 --> 00:07:56,240
I've repeatedly reviewed

177
00:07:56,240 --> 00:07:57,120
his case files,

178
00:07:58,100 --> 00:07:59,270
and no matter how I've analyzed the case,

179
00:07:59,270 --> 00:08:01,000
it just doesn't look like rape.

180
00:08:03,920 --> 00:08:05,180
What are your reasons?

181
00:08:06,310 --> 00:08:07,240
These two people

182
00:08:07,240 --> 00:08:09,390
maintained a relationship
for at least over a year.

183
00:08:09,390 --> 00:08:11,390
What's more,
the teachers and colleagues at the school

184
00:08:11,390 --> 00:08:12,720
found out about it quite a long time ago.

185
00:08:12,720 --> 00:08:13,390
Moreover, every time

186
00:08:13,390 --> 00:08:14,390
he went to the victim's place,

187
00:08:14,390 --> 00:08:15,680
he would stay there for several hours.

188
00:08:15,680 --> 00:08:17,040
Sometimes,
he would even stay there overnight.

189
00:08:17,040 --> 00:08:17,750
Just think about it.

190
00:08:17,750 --> 00:08:19,410
How could there be such a rape?

191
00:08:24,750 --> 00:08:25,920
The last time they did it,

192
00:08:25,920 --> 00:08:27,380
his wife discovered them.

193
00:08:27,630 --> 00:08:29,040
The girl felt ashamed.

194
00:08:29,560 --> 00:08:32,429
Stuck in a negative mindset,
she committed suicide by drinking poison.

195
00:08:32,429 --> 00:08:34,760
But this kind of thing isn't rare, either.

196
00:08:35,130 --> 00:08:36,760
Li Xiang, what do you mean?

197
00:08:36,789 --> 00:08:37,960
T-That girl

198
00:08:38,840 --> 00:08:39,570
deserved it?

199
00:08:39,750 --> 00:08:40,350
No, no, no.

200
00:08:40,870 --> 00:08:42,240
I absolutely don't mean that.

201
00:08:42,240 --> 00:08:43,440
Qiao Zhiliang

202
00:08:43,549 --> 00:08:44,950
is absolutely a scumbag.

203
00:08:46,550 --> 00:08:48,750
But the law is the law.

204
00:08:51,150 --> 00:08:53,410
Try to put it simply.
I don't quite understand it.

205
00:08:53,410 --> 00:08:55,550
The procuratorate
initiated a public prosecution

206
00:08:55,550 --> 00:08:57,320
for rape resulting in death.

207
00:08:58,910 --> 00:08:59,600
Rape

208
00:09:00,030 --> 00:09:00,760
or adultery.

209
00:09:00,910 --> 00:09:02,480
That's just one word's difference,

210
00:09:02,480 --> 00:09:04,610
but it concerns a man's life and death.

211
00:09:06,360 --> 00:09:06,870
So,

212
00:09:07,670 --> 00:09:09,130
he doesn't deserve to die?

213
00:09:11,720 --> 00:09:12,960
In the court of morality,

214
00:09:12,960 --> 00:09:14,020
he deserves to die.

215
00:09:14,550 --> 00:09:15,840
But in a real court,

216
00:09:17,120 --> 00:09:18,840
I think we...

217
00:09:18,860 --> 00:09:19,910
Alright, alright.

218
00:09:19,910 --> 00:09:21,970
You don't need to explain it anymore.

219
00:09:26,000 --> 00:09:27,060
You're saying that

220
00:09:27,360 --> 00:09:29,030
even if he's a scumbag,

221
00:09:29,910 --> 00:09:32,170
he still has the right to defend himself.

222
00:09:32,360 --> 00:09:34,020
If he wants to defend himself,

223
00:09:34,790 --> 00:09:35,850
we have to help him.

224
00:09:35,910 --> 00:09:37,110
Is that what you mean?

225
00:09:38,480 --> 00:09:38,870
Yes.

226
00:09:49,770 --> 00:09:51,700
His family is from the city, right?

227
00:09:51,870 --> 00:09:53,000
So you've sensed it?

228
00:09:53,910 --> 00:09:55,570
He's from a family of lawyers.

229
00:09:56,120 --> 00:09:57,250
What does that mean?

230
00:09:57,630 --> 00:09:58,830
It's a family legacy.

231
00:09:59,320 --> 00:10:00,000
Since childhood, he has known that

232
00:10:00,000 --> 00:10:01,800
he wants to be a presiding judge.

233
00:10:14,550 --> 00:10:15,280
You're back.

234
00:10:18,150 --> 00:10:19,350
Did you get anything?

235
00:10:20,200 --> 00:10:22,730
After working for a whole day,
we got nothing.

236
00:10:23,510 --> 00:10:23,970
Mentor.

237
00:10:24,510 --> 00:10:25,390
I think the criminal elements

238
00:10:25,390 --> 00:10:27,450
of this case are basically complete.

239
00:10:27,630 --> 00:10:28,390
If you still think that

240
00:10:28,390 --> 00:10:29,870
the main facts are unclear,

241
00:10:29,870 --> 00:10:31,550
we can return it to the procuratorate
for supplementary investigation

242
00:10:31,550 --> 00:10:33,150
and to gather more evidence.

243
00:10:33,320 --> 00:10:34,460
What are criminal elements?

244
00:10:34,460 --> 00:10:35,240
You've never studied law before.

245
00:10:35,240 --> 00:10:37,630
I can't explain it to you clearly
with a few words.

246
00:10:37,630 --> 00:10:38,150
Mentor.

247
00:10:38,720 --> 00:10:40,320
With the evidence we currently have,

248
00:10:40,320 --> 00:10:41,780
we can actually acquit him

249
00:10:42,000 --> 00:10:43,730
due to insufficient evidence.

250
00:10:52,910 --> 00:10:53,970
I'm going home now.

251
00:11:05,960 --> 00:11:06,670
What was he

252
00:11:07,360 --> 00:11:08,560
laughing at just now?

253
00:11:08,760 --> 00:11:11,690
He was laughing at our naivety.
What else could it be?

254
00:11:12,240 --> 00:11:13,840
Are we still going tomorrow?

255
00:11:14,000 --> 00:11:14,720
I'm not going tomorrow.

256
00:11:14,720 --> 00:11:15,960
I need to make a long-distance call home.

257
00:11:15,960 --> 00:11:17,490
There's something urgent.

258
00:11:17,750 --> 00:11:19,240
I also have something to do tomorrow.

259
00:11:19,240 --> 00:11:20,480
There's a task from Court Pres. Ding.

260
00:11:20,480 --> 00:11:22,140
Let's leave it at that for now.

261
00:11:26,910 --> 00:11:28,360
I've noticed that you seem a bit hostile

262
00:11:28,360 --> 00:11:29,360
to Zheng Jianmin.

263
00:11:29,510 --> 00:11:30,510
Did he offend you?

264
00:11:30,630 --> 00:11:31,320
Today, he told me

265
00:11:31,320 --> 00:11:32,580
he wanted to be a judge.

266
00:11:34,270 --> 00:11:34,910
If it consists of all these people

267
00:11:34,910 --> 00:11:37,440
who switch professions halfway
and make efforts at the last minute,

268
00:11:37,440 --> 00:11:38,120
when will China's legal system

269
00:11:38,120 --> 00:11:39,380
get on the right track?

270
00:11:40,270 --> 00:11:41,600
I don't have the guts to criticize him.

271
00:11:41,600 --> 00:11:43,290
You think you don't have the guts
to criticize him?

272
00:11:43,290 --> 00:11:46,150
You almost accused him
of being ignorant of the law.

273
00:11:46,480 --> 00:11:47,740
Where's Chen Yizhong?

274
00:11:49,000 --> 00:11:49,460
Mentor!

275
00:11:49,910 --> 00:11:51,310
Mentor! Mentor! Mentor!

276
00:11:51,720 --> 00:11:52,360
Lu.

277
00:11:52,870 --> 00:11:53,510
No, Yu.

278
00:11:55,000 --> 00:11:55,510
Chen.

279
00:11:57,960 --> 00:11:59,200
Chen, Chen.

280
00:11:59,510 --> 00:12:00,150
Chen Yizhong.

281
00:12:00,150 --> 00:12:00,510
Yes.

282
00:12:01,120 --> 00:12:02,890
Several interns joined us all at once.

283
00:12:02,890 --> 00:12:04,790
I can't tell you guys apart for a moment.

284
00:12:04,790 --> 00:12:05,510
What's the matter?

285
00:12:05,510 --> 00:12:05,970
Mentor.

286
00:12:06,200 --> 00:12:07,000
I'd like to ask

287
00:12:07,200 --> 00:12:08,110
whether you don't think

288
00:12:08,110 --> 00:12:10,110
Liu Erlin's case was robbery at all.

289
00:12:11,390 --> 00:12:12,240
Are you saying

290
00:12:13,440 --> 00:12:14,540
I'm intentionally covering for him?

291
00:12:14,540 --> 00:12:15,340
Of course not.

292
00:12:15,750 --> 00:12:16,230
I know.

293
00:12:16,750 --> 00:12:18,210
You guys watched the trial

294
00:12:18,510 --> 00:12:20,840
and think us people
in the grassroots court

295
00:12:20,840 --> 00:12:21,840
don't know the law

296
00:12:22,030 --> 00:12:23,590
and are unprofessional with no principles,

297
00:12:23,590 --> 00:12:24,980
merely messing around.

298
00:12:25,010 --> 00:12:26,470
No, that's not what I mean.

299
00:12:27,390 --> 00:12:29,360
Liu Erlin is indeed a loafer.

300
00:12:30,430 --> 00:12:32,690
But to say he had the guts
to rob others...

301
00:12:34,550 --> 00:12:35,910
If you say I'm prejudiced
by first impressions,

302
00:12:35,910 --> 00:12:36,770
maybe a little.

303
00:12:37,120 --> 00:12:38,850
But to say I'm covering for him,

304
00:12:39,670 --> 00:12:40,600
I wouldn't dare.

305
00:12:41,360 --> 00:12:42,890
It's a critical period now.

306
00:12:42,910 --> 00:12:45,570
We're cracking down hard
on criminal offenses.

307
00:12:45,600 --> 00:12:47,670
If I'm too lenient or too strict,

308
00:12:49,490 --> 00:12:50,080
it might affect

309
00:12:50,080 --> 00:12:51,340
a person's whole life.

310
00:12:53,910 --> 00:12:54,870
Then what if...

311
00:12:56,030 --> 00:12:57,150
What if we can't

312
00:12:57,150 --> 00:12:58,610
find new witnesses later?

313
00:13:00,720 --> 00:13:03,000
Then just let him imprisoned
for the rest of his life.

314
00:13:03,000 --> 00:13:04,060
Let him rot in jail.

315
00:13:04,320 --> 00:13:06,390
Aren't you contradicting yourself?

316
00:13:07,320 --> 00:13:07,780
Mentor.

317
00:13:08,270 --> 00:13:09,150
I think it's precisely because

318
00:13:09,150 --> 00:13:10,000
of this period

319
00:13:10,240 --> 00:13:11,120
that we should make more efforts

320
00:13:11,120 --> 00:13:12,920
to prove Liu Erlin's innocence.

321
00:13:14,150 --> 00:13:15,120
How do you know

322
00:13:15,120 --> 00:13:16,150
he's innocent?

323
00:13:16,840 --> 00:13:18,840
Just because of a few words I said to you?

324
00:13:18,840 --> 00:13:19,200
No.

325
00:13:20,030 --> 00:13:21,750
Before the court finds him guilty,

326
00:13:21,750 --> 00:13:23,020
I presume every defendant

327
00:13:23,020 --> 00:13:23,850
is innocent.

328
00:13:24,790 --> 00:13:25,630
Presume?

329
00:13:25,720 --> 00:13:26,150
Right.

330
00:13:29,080 --> 00:13:30,680
If this presumption of yours

331
00:13:30,780 --> 00:13:31,790
is stated in court,

332
00:13:31,790 --> 00:13:33,120
at this current period,

333
00:13:34,080 --> 00:13:35,880
it's not much louder than a fart.

334
00:13:37,960 --> 00:13:39,100
If you think it's troublesome,

335
00:13:39,100 --> 00:13:40,830
you don't have to go look for it.

336
00:13:41,120 --> 00:13:42,240
He's just unlucky.

337
00:13:54,180 --> 00:13:58,190
[Nanyu County Detention Center]

338
00:14:01,550 --> 00:14:02,480
Why do you have to

339
00:14:02,550 --> 00:14:03,440
defend him?

340
00:14:04,680 --> 00:14:05,740
Hey, wait a minute!

341
00:14:05,960 --> 00:14:06,690
What is this?

342
00:14:08,440 --> 00:14:09,640
It's just a recorder.

343
00:14:09,970 --> 00:14:11,240
Are you from the TV station

344
00:14:11,240 --> 00:14:12,900
or the Legal Advisory Office?

345
00:14:13,750 --> 00:14:14,480
I'm a lawyer.

346
00:14:16,220 --> 00:14:16,600
This equipment

347
00:14:16,600 --> 00:14:18,060
can't be used in our place.

348
00:14:21,030 --> 00:14:21,560
Comrade.

349
00:14:22,320 --> 00:14:24,200
I'm coming here alone to see my client.

350
00:14:24,200 --> 00:14:25,550
I'll just record the process.

351
00:14:25,550 --> 00:14:27,120
If something happens later,

352
00:14:27,120 --> 00:14:28,520
this can also protect us.

353
00:14:29,030 --> 00:14:30,830
Then I have to ask my supervisor.

354
00:14:32,510 --> 00:14:33,370
Then go ask him.

355
00:14:58,600 --> 00:14:59,860
Hello, Qiao Zhiliang.

356
00:15:00,750 --> 00:15:01,810
My name is Li Xiang.

357
00:15:01,960 --> 00:15:03,840
The Legal Advisory Office sent me here

358
00:15:03,840 --> 00:15:04,840
to be your lawyer.

359
00:15:06,750 --> 00:15:07,750
Do you agree

360
00:15:08,510 --> 00:15:10,040
to entrust me to defend you?

361
00:15:14,720 --> 00:15:15,780
Quit defending me.

362
00:15:18,240 --> 00:15:19,100
Qiao Zhiliang.

363
00:15:19,320 --> 00:15:20,320
Here's the thing.

364
00:15:20,750 --> 00:15:22,080
The law stipulates that

365
00:15:22,200 --> 00:15:24,240
cases with a potential death penalty

366
00:15:24,240 --> 00:15:26,120
must have a defender.

367
00:15:34,000 --> 00:15:36,080
Here is the Defense Authorization Letter.

368
00:15:36,080 --> 00:15:36,810
If you agree,

369
00:15:37,390 --> 00:15:38,120
just sign it.

370
00:15:48,720 --> 00:15:49,750
The indictment

371
00:15:49,960 --> 00:15:50,750
accuses you

372
00:15:51,200 --> 00:15:52,800
of raping your wife's niece,

373
00:15:53,320 --> 00:15:54,080
Wei Sanmei.

374
00:15:54,240 --> 00:15:55,170
Regarding this,

375
00:15:55,600 --> 00:15:57,130
do you have anything to say?

376
00:16:04,120 --> 00:16:04,550
No.

377
00:16:07,720 --> 00:16:08,600
So you

378
00:16:09,030 --> 00:16:10,430
admit that you raped her?

379
00:16:19,200 --> 00:16:20,510
Was it rape

380
00:16:21,120 --> 00:16:21,960
or adultery?

381
00:16:27,510 --> 00:16:28,440
Five kids?

382
00:16:31,390 --> 00:16:31,910
That judge

383
00:16:31,910 --> 00:16:33,370
brought five kids to work.

384
00:16:33,790 --> 00:16:35,520
If the litigants had seen that,

385
00:16:36,510 --> 00:16:37,870
how much would the judge's authority

386
00:16:37,870 --> 00:16:38,840
be affected?

387
00:16:40,720 --> 00:16:42,380
I even helped change a diaper.

388
00:16:42,630 --> 00:16:43,360
I was clumsy

389
00:16:43,390 --> 00:16:45,590
and got the baby's poop all over my hand.

390
00:16:49,200 --> 00:16:49,600
Oh, right.

391
00:16:49,600 --> 00:16:50,530
It was this hand.

392
00:16:50,560 --> 00:16:51,710
Smell it. Does it stink?

393
00:16:51,710 --> 00:16:52,170
Come on.

394
00:16:52,470 --> 00:16:53,120
I don't have the habit

395
00:16:53,120 --> 00:16:54,580
of having congee at night.

396
00:16:57,240 --> 00:16:57,870
What's more, she even

397
00:16:57,870 --> 00:16:59,440
graduated from Xihua University
of Political Science and Law.

398
00:16:59,440 --> 00:17:01,240
That's what makes it such a pity.

399
00:17:01,580 --> 00:17:02,770
As a graduate of Xihua University
of Political Science and Law,

400
00:17:02,770 --> 00:17:03,580
she came back here to have five kids.

401
00:17:03,580 --> 00:17:05,200
Her college education was a waste.

402
00:17:05,200 --> 00:17:07,240
But her professional skills
are very strong.

403
00:17:07,240 --> 00:17:08,880
There are no cases for her to try today.

404
00:17:08,880 --> 00:17:09,510
But she brought the kids

405
00:17:09,510 --> 00:17:11,040
and read case files all day.

406
00:17:11,440 --> 00:17:12,880
She even met with two litigants.

407
00:17:12,880 --> 00:17:13,280
Right?

408
00:17:14,359 --> 00:17:15,750
She's quite good at reading case files.

409
00:17:15,750 --> 00:17:16,720
By reading through a file just once,

410
00:17:16,720 --> 00:17:17,750
she can summarize all the key points

411
00:17:17,750 --> 00:17:18,880
in the file clearly.

412
00:17:19,109 --> 00:17:19,940
In the same time,

413
00:17:19,940 --> 00:17:20,589
she can also identify

414
00:17:20,589 --> 00:17:21,920
all the problems in the file clearly.

415
00:17:21,920 --> 00:17:23,180
It's very incredible.

416
00:17:23,920 --> 00:17:25,380
Let's observe her for now.

417
00:17:25,599 --> 00:17:26,720
If it's really not okay,
I'll tell Court Pres. Ding

418
00:17:26,720 --> 00:17:27,319
about this

419
00:17:27,720 --> 00:17:28,960
to change your mentor.

420
00:17:28,960 --> 00:17:30,160
We're here to be interns,

421
00:17:30,160 --> 00:17:31,420
not to change diapers.

422
00:17:32,200 --> 00:17:33,000
I don't want that.

423
00:17:33,000 --> 00:17:34,730
We just like changing diapers.

424
00:17:35,680 --> 00:17:37,410
I shouldn't have suggested it.

425
00:17:38,200 --> 00:17:40,060
They just want to change diapers.

426
00:17:41,360 --> 00:17:46,570
[Nanyu County People's Court,
People's Procuratorate]

427
00:17:46,920 --> 00:17:47,590
Today,

428
00:17:47,590 --> 00:17:49,240
we are looking at a murder case.

429
00:17:49,240 --> 00:17:50,640
The defendant, Qiu Agui,

430
00:17:50,970 --> 00:17:51,930
was not even 17

431
00:17:51,960 --> 00:17:53,790
when her parents
made her engaged to someone.

432
00:17:53,790 --> 00:17:55,200
Their purpose was to trade their daughter
for a bride price

433
00:17:55,200 --> 00:17:57,640
so that her younger brother
could use it to get married.

434
00:17:57,640 --> 00:17:58,920
At that time, her brother

435
00:17:58,920 --> 00:17:59,960
wasn't even 14.

436
00:18:05,350 --> 00:18:06,550
In rural Nanyu,

437
00:18:06,570 --> 00:18:07,440
husbands beating their wives

438
00:18:07,440 --> 00:18:08,410
is quite common.

439
00:18:09,350 --> 00:18:11,030
After Qiu Agui got married,

440
00:18:11,350 --> 00:18:13,150
she was beaten on the second day.

441
00:18:14,030 --> 00:18:15,480
She was beaten continuously

442
00:18:15,480 --> 00:18:16,830
until she became a mother
of three children.

443
00:18:16,830 --> 00:18:19,090
Believe it or not, I'll beat you to death!

444
00:18:19,420 --> 00:18:20,160
As for when exactly

445
00:18:20,160 --> 00:18:20,920
Qiu Agui got

446
00:18:20,940 --> 00:18:21,660
this idea,

447
00:18:22,350 --> 00:18:24,680
she probably
couldn't even explain it well herself.

448
00:18:24,680 --> 00:18:26,480
But with even just a little hope,

449
00:18:26,720 --> 00:18:29,180
a person
wouldn't take this desperate path.

450
00:18:29,750 --> 00:18:32,200
Mom, I'm scared!

451
00:18:33,310 --> 00:18:34,240
Don't be scared.

452
00:18:34,480 --> 00:18:35,240
Your dad

453
00:18:35,510 --> 00:18:36,770
won't beat us anymore.

454
00:19:00,830 --> 00:19:02,030
I killed my husband.

455
00:19:07,310 --> 00:19:09,110
The procuratorate
suggested the death penalty.

456
00:19:09,110 --> 00:19:09,640
It's been pending for my decision

457
00:19:09,640 --> 00:19:10,500
for two months.

458
00:19:11,920 --> 00:19:12,400
Mentor,

459
00:19:12,400 --> 00:19:13,590
this is a county-level court.

460
00:19:13,590 --> 00:19:15,160
Can we also try death penalty cases?

461
00:19:15,160 --> 00:19:16,690
We couldn't do that before.

462
00:19:17,350 --> 00:19:19,270
But aren't we
in the Strike-Hard Campaign now?

463
00:19:19,270 --> 00:19:20,600
So county-level courts

464
00:19:21,200 --> 00:19:22,510
can also try death penalty cases.

465
00:19:22,510 --> 00:19:23,350
The power of death penalty review

466
00:19:23,350 --> 00:19:24,810
used to be owned by the Supreme Court.

467
00:19:24,810 --> 00:19:26,640
Now it's been delegated
to the province-level courts.

468
00:19:26,640 --> 00:19:27,750
It's been so many years

469
00:19:27,750 --> 00:19:29,200
since the founding of New China.

470
00:19:29,200 --> 00:19:30,550
How can people
still trade their own daughters

471
00:19:30,550 --> 00:19:31,550
for bride prices?

472
00:19:34,840 --> 00:19:36,100
Because they are poor.

473
00:19:39,480 --> 00:19:39,880
Yes.

474
00:19:41,520 --> 00:19:42,680
The most tragic victims

475
00:19:42,680 --> 00:19:43,920
of poverty and wars are usually

476
00:19:43,920 --> 00:19:45,310
women and children.

477
00:19:46,480 --> 00:19:47,880
To improve women's fate,

478
00:19:48,000 --> 00:19:49,730
we need to start with improving

479
00:19:49,750 --> 00:19:51,080
economy and education.

480
00:19:51,270 --> 00:19:53,030
Our mentor graduated from Xihua University
of Political Science and Law.

481
00:19:53,030 --> 00:19:54,030
Isn't she back...

482
00:20:07,720 --> 00:20:09,180
Well, what did Zhang mean?

483
00:20:09,790 --> 00:20:11,790
He didn't elaborate on the details,

484
00:20:11,960 --> 00:20:14,090
just waiting for us to run our legs off.

485
00:20:15,160 --> 00:20:17,340
Actually, what he said was very simple.

486
00:20:17,340 --> 00:20:18,230
Just one word—

487
00:20:18,440 --> 00:20:19,040
evidence.

488
00:20:20,550 --> 00:20:21,270
We've been overlooking

489
00:20:21,270 --> 00:20:22,400
one thing all along.

490
00:20:22,640 --> 00:20:24,840
Liu Erlin said
he mistook the person for someone else.

491
00:20:24,840 --> 00:20:25,830
But as for who he mistook that person for,

492
00:20:25,830 --> 00:20:26,920
we don't know about it.

493
00:20:26,920 --> 00:20:27,320
Right?

494
00:20:28,070 --> 00:20:29,110
If we can find this person,

495
00:20:29,110 --> 00:20:30,640
it might be a breakthrough.

496
00:20:30,960 --> 00:20:32,550
Will the court accept it?

497
00:20:33,680 --> 00:20:34,720
There are still two words—

498
00:20:34,720 --> 00:20:35,920
inner conviction.

499
00:20:36,440 --> 00:20:37,130
If we find this person

500
00:20:37,130 --> 00:20:38,270
and compare the two people,

501
00:20:38,270 --> 00:20:39,510
confirming that their backs
really look alike,

502
00:20:39,510 --> 00:20:40,400
then Liu Erlin was probably

503
00:20:40,400 --> 00:20:41,530
just joking, right?

504
00:20:41,640 --> 00:20:42,590
And then with the other factors

505
00:20:42,590 --> 00:20:43,320
in this case,

506
00:20:43,440 --> 00:20:44,720
we can basically confirm

507
00:20:44,720 --> 00:20:46,440
that Liu Erlin was just joking,

508
00:20:46,440 --> 00:20:47,880
so he can't be sentenced for robbery.

509
00:20:47,880 --> 00:20:48,550
Alright.

510
00:20:48,570 --> 00:20:49,400
Stop playing

511
00:20:49,420 --> 00:20:50,240
word games with me.

512
00:20:50,240 --> 00:20:50,980
Just tell me

513
00:20:51,200 --> 00:20:52,200
what Zhang meant.

514
00:20:52,920 --> 00:20:54,000
He's just like an old fox.

515
00:20:54,000 --> 00:20:54,640
And what about Yu Gaoyuan?

516
00:20:54,640 --> 00:20:55,640
Why isn't he here?

517
00:20:55,800 --> 00:20:57,240
Does he think this case is too small

518
00:20:57,240 --> 00:20:58,350
and too troublesome?

519
00:20:58,350 --> 00:20:59,070
He's so sly.

520
00:20:59,750 --> 00:21:01,000
Something came up at his home, didn't it?

521
00:21:01,000 --> 00:21:03,060
He couldn't come even if he wanted to.

522
00:21:24,200 --> 00:21:24,880
Let's go.

523
00:21:29,270 --> 00:21:30,750
Even if you can't save Du Xiaohui,

524
00:21:30,750 --> 00:21:32,480
at least you can save yourself.

525
00:21:33,270 --> 00:21:36,270
This incident will haunt you
for the rest of your life.

526
00:21:37,350 --> 00:21:37,810
Come on.

527
00:21:40,640 --> 00:21:41,440
Let's go back.

528
00:21:45,050 --> 00:21:46,350
Which place are we going back to?

529
00:21:46,350 --> 00:21:47,790
Let's go back and keep asking.

530
00:21:47,790 --> 00:21:48,790
Even if it might take a year
to ask about it,

531
00:21:48,790 --> 00:21:50,000
we still need to find the witness.

532
00:21:50,000 --> 00:21:50,530
Let's go.

533
00:21:50,880 --> 00:21:51,160
Well,

534
00:21:51,160 --> 00:21:53,220
we've already asked up to 100 people.

535
00:21:54,210 --> 00:21:54,830
During this one-year internship,

536
00:21:54,830 --> 00:21:57,290
we have to look for witnesses
for half a year?

537
00:21:59,270 --> 00:22:01,270
He was just joking with that person.

538
00:22:02,030 --> 00:22:03,030
Liu Erlin's brain

539
00:22:03,030 --> 00:22:04,400
doesn't work well.

540
00:22:04,750 --> 00:22:07,010
It's like something is missing up there.

541
00:22:07,440 --> 00:22:08,170
If you ask me,

542
00:22:08,450 --> 00:22:09,070
it's good to put him in jail

543
00:22:09,070 --> 00:22:11,730
and teach him a lesson there
for a couple of days.

544
00:22:12,640 --> 00:22:13,240
Are you...

545
00:22:13,440 --> 00:22:14,500
Are you a reporter?

546
00:22:14,730 --> 00:22:16,010
No, I'm from the court.

547
00:22:18,550 --> 00:22:19,810
Wasn't he just joking?

548
00:22:20,350 --> 00:22:22,030
Is it so serious that he'll be sentenced?

549
00:22:22,030 --> 00:22:23,920
It depends on how the case is classified.

550
00:22:23,920 --> 00:22:25,650
If it's considered as robbery,

551
00:22:26,000 --> 00:22:27,420
he'll be sentenced to 15 years.

552
00:22:27,420 --> 00:22:28,400
If he was just joking,

553
00:22:28,400 --> 00:22:30,330
he'll just be detained for 15 days.

554
00:22:36,590 --> 00:22:37,000
Bro.

555
00:22:37,590 --> 00:22:38,790
You just said Liu Erlin

556
00:22:38,790 --> 00:22:40,480
might have mistaken the person
for someone else.

557
00:22:40,480 --> 00:22:41,940
Who did he mistake him for?

558
00:22:42,480 --> 00:22:43,640
I'm thinking

559
00:22:45,510 --> 00:22:46,840
whether it was Laishun.

560
00:22:47,000 --> 00:22:47,680
Laishun?

561
00:22:48,750 --> 00:22:50,410
Liu Erlin always bullied him.

562
00:22:52,240 --> 00:22:53,900
Where does this Laishun live?

563
00:22:55,440 --> 00:22:56,040
He's dead.

564
00:22:58,960 --> 00:22:59,980
A couple of days ago,

565
00:22:59,980 --> 00:23:01,510
he was run over and killed by a big truck

566
00:23:01,510 --> 00:23:03,240
that was transporting timber.

567
00:23:05,200 --> 00:23:06,000
Who's dead?

568
00:23:13,150 --> 00:23:13,880
You're all here.

569
00:23:13,880 --> 00:23:14,590
Sit down.

570
00:23:14,590 --> 00:23:16,720
-Court Pres. Ding.
-Court Pres. Ding.

571
00:23:17,590 --> 00:23:18,390
I'm wondering

572
00:23:18,920 --> 00:23:20,440
when Qiu Agui's case

573
00:23:21,200 --> 00:23:22,440
will go to trial.

574
00:23:25,790 --> 00:23:28,000
Can we
get a suspended death sentence for her?

575
00:23:28,000 --> 00:23:29,320
Their father is already dead.

576
00:23:29,320 --> 00:23:31,520
Let's leave a mother for the three kids.

577
00:23:34,160 --> 00:23:34,920
Fang Shumei,

578
00:23:35,640 --> 00:23:37,840
could you just see how the situation is?

579
00:23:38,480 --> 00:23:41,030
Her husband's family
gathered dozens of people

580
00:23:41,030 --> 00:23:43,890
to make trouble
at the county government every day.

581
00:23:44,720 --> 00:23:45,250
Alright.

582
00:23:45,720 --> 00:23:46,450
Look at this.

583
00:23:48,400 --> 00:23:49,930
They've even sent us a letter
written in blood.

584
00:23:49,930 --> 00:23:50,920
The county government

585
00:23:50,920 --> 00:23:52,520
keeps calling us like crazy.

586
00:23:52,590 --> 00:23:53,790
If we don't convict her soon,

587
00:23:53,790 --> 00:23:54,960
there will be chaos.

588
00:23:57,920 --> 00:23:59,830
This is intentional homicide.

589
00:24:00,590 --> 00:24:01,790
But Court Pres. Ding,

590
00:24:01,790 --> 00:24:03,750
I understand
she was afraid of being beaten to death.

591
00:24:03,750 --> 00:24:05,490
She struck first
because she was so terrified.

592
00:24:05,490 --> 00:24:06,650
Strictly speaking,

593
00:24:06,680 --> 00:24:09,340
it could be considered
as justifiable defense.

594
00:24:12,880 --> 00:24:14,160
It looks like I'm still

595
00:24:14,510 --> 00:24:16,570
lacking in professional knowledge.

596
00:24:17,720 --> 00:24:19,030
Alright, Young Comrade.

597
00:24:19,030 --> 00:24:19,490
Come on.

598
00:24:19,680 --> 00:24:20,940
Explain to me

599
00:24:21,160 --> 00:24:22,820
what justifiable defense is.

600
00:24:23,230 --> 00:24:25,020
Justifiable defense means...

601
00:24:25,040 --> 00:24:26,590
When her husband was drunk,

602
00:24:27,350 --> 00:24:29,080
she hacked him dozens of times,

603
00:24:29,880 --> 00:24:31,540
chopping off half of his face,

604
00:24:32,270 --> 00:24:33,880
which even made him unrecognizable.

605
00:24:33,880 --> 00:24:34,920
So this is justifiable defense?

606
00:24:34,920 --> 00:24:36,250
Is it, college student?

607
00:24:43,400 --> 00:24:44,110
Court Pres. Ding.

608
00:24:44,110 --> 00:24:44,510
Speak.

609
00:24:45,240 --> 00:24:46,700
Considering that her husband

610
00:24:46,700 --> 00:24:48,080
often beat her up,

611
00:24:48,270 --> 00:24:50,330
can we give her a lighter punishment?

612
00:24:53,830 --> 00:24:55,830
You've received so much education.

613
00:24:56,590 --> 00:24:58,720
Have you ever taken a lesson like this?

614
00:24:59,590 --> 00:25:01,350
That is, when the law

615
00:25:01,640 --> 00:25:03,070
cannot be separated from

616
00:25:03,120 --> 00:25:04,720
social reality,

617
00:25:06,550 --> 00:25:07,550
what should we do?

618
00:25:09,680 --> 00:25:11,880
The so-called social reality
you've mentioned

619
00:25:11,880 --> 00:25:12,590
is that men

620
00:25:12,590 --> 00:25:13,730
can beat their wives up as they please,

621
00:25:13,730 --> 00:25:14,830
but once women resist,

622
00:25:14,830 --> 00:25:16,830
they will be punished by law, right?

623
00:25:17,350 --> 00:25:19,350
The social reality here in our place

624
00:25:20,510 --> 00:25:21,400
is poverty

625
00:25:22,270 --> 00:25:23,600
and underdevelopment.

626
00:25:24,200 --> 00:25:25,000
Many men

627
00:25:25,880 --> 00:25:26,950
would beat their wives.

628
00:25:26,950 --> 00:25:28,080
You can't say that.

629
00:25:28,160 --> 00:25:29,160
Stop, stop, stop.

630
00:25:29,420 --> 00:25:31,150
I know what you're going to say.

631
00:25:32,250 --> 00:25:33,170
Of course I know

632
00:25:33,200 --> 00:25:34,260
this is a bad habit.

633
00:25:37,550 --> 00:25:38,810
I have always believed

634
00:25:39,640 --> 00:25:40,760
that men who beat their wives

635
00:25:40,760 --> 00:25:41,890
are all scumbags,

636
00:25:41,920 --> 00:25:43,720
and they should all be arrested.

637
00:25:44,240 --> 00:25:45,700
I've said that, haven't I?

638
00:25:46,010 --> 00:25:47,410
You've always said that.

639
00:25:48,160 --> 00:25:49,360
But don't forget that

640
00:25:49,640 --> 00:25:51,750
this concept and such behavior

641
00:25:52,400 --> 00:25:53,660
cannot be changed by us

642
00:25:53,680 --> 00:25:54,720
in a short term.

643
00:25:55,720 --> 00:25:57,520
Isn't this also social reality?

644
00:26:02,310 --> 00:26:03,510
Currently, the situation

645
00:26:03,510 --> 00:26:04,680
is already like this.

646
00:26:04,680 --> 00:26:05,740
Let me tell you all.

647
00:26:06,350 --> 00:26:07,350
If we don't sentence her

648
00:26:07,350 --> 00:26:08,880
to death in this case,

649
00:26:09,550 --> 00:26:11,860
in the future,
there might be more and more incidents

650
00:26:11,860 --> 00:26:13,720
of wives hacking their husbands.

651
00:26:14,720 --> 00:26:15,590
This logic is twisted

652
00:26:15,590 --> 00:26:16,420
so greatly.

653
00:26:16,480 --> 00:26:17,750
Why don't you say Qiu Agui

654
00:26:17,750 --> 00:26:18,800
made an example of him

655
00:26:18,800 --> 00:26:19,590
so that those scumbags

656
00:26:19,590 --> 00:26:21,460
would never
dare to beat their wives again?

657
00:26:21,460 --> 00:26:21,880
Well, she...

658
00:26:21,880 --> 00:26:22,440
Court Pres. Ding.

659
00:26:22,440 --> 00:26:23,640
She doesn't mean you're twisted.

660
00:26:23,640 --> 00:26:24,640
Isn't he twisted?

661
00:26:27,070 --> 00:26:28,070
Isn't he twisted?

662
00:26:29,310 --> 00:26:30,330
He's just twisted.

663
00:26:30,330 --> 00:26:31,530
Um, does this mean...

664
00:26:32,310 --> 00:26:33,590
Twisted.

665
00:26:34,590 --> 00:26:35,650
I'm twisted, okay?

666
00:26:37,110 --> 00:26:38,910
I... I can't outdebate you guys.

667
00:26:40,030 --> 00:26:41,690
As for the current situation,

668
00:26:42,030 --> 00:26:43,230
you all know about it.

669
00:26:43,790 --> 00:26:44,520
Fang Shumei.

670
00:26:45,790 --> 00:26:46,920
Handle it yourself.

671
00:26:51,830 --> 00:26:52,360
Ms. Fang.

672
00:26:53,590 --> 00:26:55,120
You're calling me Ms. Fang?

673
00:26:56,400 --> 00:26:57,330
Is that strange?

674
00:26:58,880 --> 00:27:01,080
You have the highest level of education

675
00:27:01,160 --> 00:27:02,110
in our court.

676
00:27:04,000 --> 00:27:04,750
Do you think

677
00:27:05,440 --> 00:27:07,370
according to the new criminal law,

678
00:27:08,240 --> 00:27:10,040
she deserves the death penalty?

679
00:27:15,480 --> 00:27:16,280
Yes, she does.

680
00:27:24,360 --> 00:27:26,070
Even if Laishun were still alive,

681
00:27:26,070 --> 00:27:28,000
and even if he looked like the victim,

682
00:27:28,000 --> 00:27:29,460
that's just an inference.

683
00:27:29,480 --> 00:27:30,000
In court,

684
00:27:30,000 --> 00:27:30,920
it can't be used as evidence.

685
00:27:30,920 --> 00:27:31,750
Since it's something so basic,

686
00:27:31,750 --> 00:27:33,150
don't you guys know that?

687
00:27:36,790 --> 00:27:39,520
Zhang is just deliberately
giving us a hard time.

688
00:27:41,160 --> 00:27:43,160
It can't be used as evidence indeed,

689
00:27:43,240 --> 00:27:44,240
but it can affect

690
00:27:44,270 --> 00:27:45,440
the fairness of the trial.

691
00:27:45,440 --> 00:27:47,040
You're using such big words.

692
00:27:47,240 --> 00:27:48,160
Hey, sir.

693
00:27:48,960 --> 00:27:49,750
Stop pacing around.

694
00:27:49,750 --> 00:27:50,400
In addition,

695
00:27:50,400 --> 00:27:52,440
why are you making so many snide remarks?

696
00:27:52,440 --> 00:27:53,880
What snide remarks did I make?

697
00:27:53,880 --> 00:27:55,030
We almost ran our legs off.

698
00:27:55,030 --> 00:27:56,090
But what did you do?

699
00:27:56,480 --> 00:27:57,360
Were you staying indoors

700
00:27:57,360 --> 00:27:58,240
and thinking about
where the Chinese legal system

701
00:27:58,240 --> 00:27:59,220
should head?

702
00:28:00,320 --> 00:28:01,110
Haven't I told you something urgent

703
00:28:01,110 --> 00:28:02,440
has come up in my family latley?

704
00:28:02,440 --> 00:28:03,110
So you're the only one with issues?

705
00:28:03,110 --> 00:28:04,770
Why do you have so many issues?

706
00:28:04,830 --> 00:28:06,880
The whole country
can't do without you, huh?

707
00:28:06,880 --> 00:28:07,680
Zeming,
I've tolerated you for a long time.

708
00:28:07,680 --> 00:28:08,160
Do you know that?

709
00:28:08,160 --> 00:28:09,680
Have I asked you to tolerate me?

710
00:28:09,680 --> 00:28:10,350
Just hit me!

711
00:28:22,030 --> 00:28:22,680
Don't you guys think

712
00:28:22,680 --> 00:28:24,010
you're are so childish?

713
00:28:28,720 --> 00:28:29,200
Um...

714
00:28:29,720 --> 00:28:31,590
Well, why is she angry?

715
00:28:35,920 --> 00:28:36,830
Today, we studied

716
00:28:36,830 --> 00:28:38,590
a husband-killing case with our mentor.

717
00:28:38,590 --> 00:28:40,270
It must have affected her mood.

718
00:28:40,270 --> 00:28:41,200
What husband-killing case?

719
00:28:41,200 --> 00:28:41,680
Why?

720
00:28:42,310 --> 00:28:44,310
Because of suffering and injustice.

721
00:28:44,310 --> 00:28:45,220
When she was in desperation,

722
00:28:45,220 --> 00:28:46,220
no one helped her.

723
00:28:46,680 --> 00:28:47,750
When she resisted,

724
00:28:48,510 --> 00:28:50,040
she was punished by the law.

725
00:28:56,350 --> 00:28:57,950
It's alright. I'm used to it.

726
00:28:59,400 --> 00:29:01,130
He always makes snide remarks.

727
00:29:04,830 --> 00:29:06,560
I know you're in a very bad mood.

728
00:29:08,110 --> 00:29:08,880
What happened?

729
00:29:08,880 --> 00:29:09,810
Tell me about it.

730
00:29:13,480 --> 00:29:14,550
It's just about the tricky issues
in the village.

731
00:29:14,550 --> 00:29:16,150
You wouldn't be interested.

732
00:29:17,070 --> 00:29:18,400
You're like this again.

733
00:29:21,550 --> 00:29:23,880
Isn't there the household contract
responsibility system?

734
00:29:23,880 --> 00:29:25,480
Our family got six mu of land.

735
00:29:25,960 --> 00:29:27,290
Only two mu of it is good.

736
00:29:27,750 --> 00:29:29,070
Now they want to exchange bad land

737
00:29:29,070 --> 00:29:30,050
for the two mu of good land.

738
00:29:30,050 --> 00:29:33,400
They say it's an exchange,
but they actually want to take it away.

739
00:29:33,400 --> 00:29:34,660
How could this happen?

740
00:29:35,160 --> 00:29:36,760
It sounds like a joke, right?

741
00:29:37,480 --> 00:29:39,340
But it's a big deal in our village.

742
00:29:39,440 --> 00:29:40,970
I called the brigade today,

743
00:29:41,550 --> 00:29:43,030
saying that I wanted to talk to my dad.

744
00:29:43,030 --> 00:29:45,890
They deliberately didn't let him
answer the phone.

745
00:29:51,590 --> 00:29:53,590
I think you should go home.

746
00:29:55,110 --> 00:29:56,440
What can I do if I go back?

747
00:29:57,070 --> 00:29:59,030
Shall I fight with the village secretary?

748
00:29:59,030 --> 00:29:59,830
No.

749
00:30:01,110 --> 00:30:02,310
As long as you go back,

750
00:30:02,920 --> 00:30:04,720
it'll be helpful to your family.

751
00:30:05,720 --> 00:30:08,120
At least it'll be a comfort
to your parents.

752
00:30:31,510 --> 00:30:32,170
Yu Gaoyuan.

753
00:30:32,830 --> 00:30:34,350
I've sterilized it with hot water.

754
00:30:34,350 --> 00:30:35,270
It's filled with cold boiled water.

755
00:30:35,270 --> 00:30:36,200
You can drink it on the way.

756
00:30:36,200 --> 00:30:36,800
Thank you.

757
00:30:37,470 --> 00:30:38,530
Take the food, too.

758
00:30:38,800 --> 00:30:39,920
They don't accept grain ration coupons
on the train.

759
00:30:39,920 --> 00:30:41,380
Buying food is expensive.

760
00:30:43,570 --> 00:30:44,400
When you go back home, do your best

761
00:30:44,400 --> 00:30:46,600
to reason with that village secretary.

762
00:30:47,220 --> 00:30:48,160
Though you have to reason with him,

763
00:30:48,160 --> 00:30:49,290
don't be impulsive.

764
00:30:50,750 --> 00:30:51,480
Don't worry.

765
00:30:52,270 --> 00:30:53,000
Zhang Lihui!

766
00:30:55,270 --> 00:30:56,200
Have a safe trip.

767
00:30:58,030 --> 00:30:58,830
What's wrong?

768
00:31:01,880 --> 00:31:02,240
Okay.

769
00:31:05,790 --> 00:31:07,520
You haven't packed much stuff.

770
00:31:08,750 --> 00:31:09,750
I can do it myself.

771
00:31:22,510 --> 00:31:23,110
Thank you.

772
00:31:23,270 --> 00:31:25,730
You were the one
who helped me make up my mind.

773
00:31:32,700 --> 00:31:33,360
Let me do it.

774
00:31:41,960 --> 00:31:42,350
Yu.

775
00:31:47,960 --> 00:31:48,690
These are...

776
00:31:49,160 --> 00:31:49,960
some national grain ration coupons.

777
00:31:49,960 --> 00:31:51,020
Take them with you.

778
00:31:52,880 --> 00:31:53,610
I'm leaving.

779
00:31:56,070 --> 00:31:57,030
Why are you giving me so many of them?

780
00:31:57,030 --> 00:31:58,480
What about you guys
if you give them to me?

781
00:31:58,480 --> 00:31:59,590
Lu collected them.

782
00:32:00,610 --> 00:32:01,990
He was too embarrassed to come himself,

783
00:32:01,990 --> 00:32:03,480
so he asked me
to apologize to you for him.

784
00:32:03,480 --> 00:32:04,740
Don't take it to heart.

785
00:32:05,120 --> 00:32:06,450
I'm not as petty as he is.

786
00:32:07,240 --> 00:32:08,790
Thanks for your help in the next few days.

787
00:32:08,790 --> 00:32:09,310
Don't worry.

788
00:32:09,310 --> 00:32:10,160
Be careful.

789
00:32:13,380 --> 00:32:14,750
Do you need to pack all this stuff?

790
00:32:14,750 --> 00:32:15,210
No need.

791
00:32:16,790 --> 00:32:17,590
Liu Bingsheng

792
00:32:17,680 --> 00:32:18,270
has been a juror here

793
00:32:18,270 --> 00:32:19,350
for three years.

794
00:32:19,510 --> 00:32:20,310
Just find him.

795
00:32:20,590 --> 00:32:21,440
He's a man.

796
00:32:25,640 --> 00:32:26,830
Not every man in Nanyu

797
00:32:26,830 --> 00:32:27,960
would beat his wife.

798
00:32:28,270 --> 00:32:29,400
At least I wouldn't.

799
00:32:29,400 --> 00:32:30,330
Are you married?

800
00:32:32,310 --> 00:32:32,720
No.

801
00:32:34,240 --> 00:32:34,970
Don't worry.

802
00:32:35,310 --> 00:32:36,960
Well, I mean, trust me.

803
00:32:37,580 --> 00:32:38,880
Just find Liu as he's the right person.

804
00:32:38,880 --> 00:32:39,210
Okay.

805
00:32:40,000 --> 00:32:40,600
Thank you.

806
00:32:41,030 --> 00:32:43,090
You're welcome. I'll get going then.

807
00:32:43,110 --> 00:32:43,550
Bye.

808
00:32:43,680 --> 00:32:44,110
Bye.

809
00:32:50,830 --> 00:32:51,630
This is yours.

810
00:32:53,310 --> 00:32:54,310
Thanks, Gaoyuan.

811
00:32:54,750 --> 00:32:55,720
This is yours.

812
00:32:56,030 --> 00:32:56,790
Take it inside the house and eat it.

813
00:32:56,790 --> 00:32:57,790
Thanks, Gaoyuan.

814
00:33:03,350 --> 00:33:05,110
Your dad is a teacher,

815
00:33:05,510 --> 00:33:07,840
but he can't even settle this small issue.

816
00:33:07,890 --> 00:33:08,790
Why did he ask you

817
00:33:08,790 --> 00:33:09,520
to come back?

818
00:33:10,270 --> 00:33:11,440
Who asked Gaoyuan to come back?

819
00:33:11,440 --> 00:33:12,200
I didn't.

820
00:33:13,110 --> 00:33:13,550
Mom.

821
00:33:14,310 --> 00:33:15,710
I came back voluntarily.

822
00:33:16,790 --> 00:33:19,050
As for my dad's issue, we're in the right.

823
00:33:19,270 --> 00:33:20,270
We have a land contract with the village

824
00:33:20,270 --> 00:33:21,520
which will remain unchanged for 15 years.

825
00:33:21,520 --> 00:33:22,440
Unless we're voluntary,

826
00:33:22,440 --> 00:33:23,790
they're just coercing us.

827
00:33:23,790 --> 00:33:25,640
The village secretary
knows he's in the wrong.

828
00:33:25,640 --> 00:33:27,590
Otherwise,
he wouldn't have used that trick.

829
00:33:27,590 --> 00:33:28,310
What trick?

830
00:33:28,720 --> 00:33:29,580
On the surface,

831
00:33:29,920 --> 00:33:31,750
the Tang family
is complaining about unfairness

832
00:33:31,750 --> 00:33:33,070
and wants to swap land with us.

833
00:33:33,070 --> 00:33:35,510
But secretly,
he's the one pulling the strings.

834
00:33:35,510 --> 00:33:36,900
After swapping land with us,
the Tang family will then

835
00:33:36,900 --> 00:33:37,960
transfer it to him.

836
00:33:37,960 --> 00:33:39,370
Everyone knows what's going on,

837
00:33:39,370 --> 00:33:40,880
but no one has the guts to point it out.

838
00:33:40,880 --> 00:33:42,880
We can only swallow the bitter pill.

839
00:33:43,590 --> 00:33:45,440
I'll go find the village secretary later.

840
00:33:45,440 --> 00:33:46,170
You can't go.

841
00:33:46,270 --> 00:33:47,270
Why can't I go?

842
00:33:47,790 --> 00:33:49,200
I'm going to reason with him,
not to fight with him.

843
00:33:49,200 --> 00:33:50,000
It's useless.

844
00:33:50,270 --> 00:33:51,750
Why are you saying that it's useless?

845
00:33:51,750 --> 00:33:53,280
It's already been swapped.

846
00:34:00,000 --> 00:34:01,400
Gaoyuan! Gaoyuan!

847
00:34:05,310 --> 00:34:06,550
Thirty-eight.

848
00:34:09,670 --> 00:34:10,670
Gaoyuan is back.

849
00:34:11,960 --> 00:34:12,510
Gaoyuan.

850
00:34:13,210 --> 00:34:14,280
You're the first college student

851
00:34:14,280 --> 00:34:16,210
in our village.

852
00:34:16,590 --> 00:34:17,940
When you went to Beijing to study...

853
00:34:17,940 --> 00:34:18,800
Let me tell you.

854
00:34:18,800 --> 00:34:19,860
I even gave your dad

855
00:34:20,070 --> 00:34:21,670
20 yuan to support you.

856
00:34:22,230 --> 00:34:22,830
Is that so?

857
00:34:23,760 --> 00:34:25,219
I'll go back and ask my dad.

858
00:34:25,500 --> 00:34:26,280
If that's true,

859
00:34:26,280 --> 00:34:28,000
we'll raise the money to return it to you.

860
00:34:28,000 --> 00:34:29,260
How could you say that?

861
00:34:29,840 --> 00:34:31,440
Come on! Have a seat!

862
00:34:31,719 --> 00:34:32,070
Sit.

863
00:34:33,280 --> 00:34:33,920
Sit down.

864
00:34:34,540 --> 00:34:35,199
Have a seat.

865
00:34:38,929 --> 00:34:40,159
I heard your family

866
00:34:40,190 --> 00:34:41,110
was allocated several mu of land.

867
00:34:41,110 --> 00:34:41,940
Four mu.

868
00:34:42,510 --> 00:34:43,030
Later,

869
00:34:43,370 --> 00:34:44,630
they insisted on swapping two mu

870
00:34:44,630 --> 00:34:45,800
with the Tang family,

871
00:34:45,800 --> 00:34:46,800
making it six mu in total.

872
00:34:46,800 --> 00:34:48,460
Aren't you talking nonsense?

873
00:34:48,590 --> 00:34:49,800
Two mu of our land was...

874
00:34:49,800 --> 00:34:50,330
Alright.

875
00:34:51,679 --> 00:34:52,550
Let's not talk about this today.

876
00:34:52,550 --> 00:34:52,960
Okay?

877
00:34:55,560 --> 00:34:56,880
What's your major in college?

878
00:34:56,880 --> 00:34:57,440
Law.

879
00:34:58,000 --> 00:34:59,260
I'm majoring in law...

880
00:35:00,180 --> 00:35:01,800
at the University
of Political Science and Law.

881
00:35:01,800 --> 00:35:02,860
After graduation,

882
00:35:03,230 --> 00:35:04,440
I can be assigned to the court

883
00:35:04,440 --> 00:35:05,700
or the procuratorate.

884
00:35:06,110 --> 00:35:07,630
I've also thought about it.

885
00:35:07,630 --> 00:35:08,690
If that's not okay,

886
00:35:08,710 --> 00:35:10,760
I'll come back to the county or the town

887
00:35:10,760 --> 00:35:12,710
and work in the judicial department.

888
00:35:12,710 --> 00:35:14,670
Village Secretary,
please look after me then.

889
00:35:14,670 --> 00:35:15,710
If you're assigned back here,

890
00:35:15,710 --> 00:35:16,800
I won't agree.

891
00:35:17,350 --> 00:35:18,340
You're so knowledgeable.

892
00:35:18,340 --> 00:35:19,110
You finally got a chance to go to Beijing

893
00:35:19,110 --> 00:35:19,960
and study at a university.

894
00:35:19,960 --> 00:35:20,480
If you come back

895
00:35:20,480 --> 00:35:21,610
to such a poor place,

896
00:35:22,150 --> 00:35:24,440
wouldn't it be a waste
of your great talents?

897
00:35:24,440 --> 00:35:25,190
In Beijing,

898
00:35:25,550 --> 00:35:27,150
you can play a bigger role.

899
00:35:27,520 --> 00:35:28,840
Whether I stay in Beijing or not
is my own business.

900
00:35:28,840 --> 00:35:30,670
Today,
we're talking about land allocation.

901
00:35:30,670 --> 00:35:31,440
Accountant Tang,

902
00:35:31,440 --> 00:35:33,230
gather the two families tomorrow

903
00:35:33,230 --> 00:35:34,490
and do as Gaoyuan says.

904
00:35:35,070 --> 00:35:37,000
Mr. Tang's three sons won't agree.

905
00:35:37,480 --> 00:35:38,840
They won't just
watch themselves suffer losses,

906
00:35:38,840 --> 00:35:39,440
will they?

907
00:35:39,480 --> 00:35:40,610
Losses are blessings.

908
00:35:40,610 --> 00:35:41,720
Who doesn't suffer losses sometimes?

909
00:35:41,720 --> 00:35:42,920
It's not about suffering losses or not.

910
00:35:42,920 --> 00:35:44,610
It's about the stipulation
of the land policy.

911
00:35:44,610 --> 00:35:45,610
Just listen to me.

912
00:35:46,190 --> 00:35:47,450
Speaking of policies,

913
00:35:48,110 --> 00:35:49,310
logically speaking,

914
00:35:49,630 --> 00:35:50,880
your dad is a teacher,

915
00:35:51,060 --> 00:35:52,040
so he shouldn't be allocated any land.

916
00:35:52,040 --> 00:35:53,150
My dad doesn't have an official position.

917
00:35:53,150 --> 00:35:53,840
He works at a private school.

918
00:35:53,840 --> 00:35:55,360
So what if he works at a private school?

919
00:35:55,360 --> 00:35:56,880
You can't have it all.

920
00:35:57,400 --> 00:35:58,510
Your dad both receives salaries
from the government

921
00:35:58,510 --> 00:36:00,230
and wants to gain an official position.

922
00:36:00,230 --> 00:36:01,510
Now you're even asking for land.

923
00:36:01,510 --> 00:36:01,880
Well,

924
00:36:01,920 --> 00:36:03,510
you guys got all the good stuff.

925
00:36:03,510 --> 00:36:04,450
As for our villagers,

926
00:36:04,450 --> 00:36:05,070
I have to give them

927
00:36:05,070 --> 00:36:06,000
an explanation.

928
00:36:06,110 --> 00:36:07,840
You used to be a student cadre, too.

929
00:36:07,840 --> 00:36:10,300
What's the most important thing
for a cadre?

930
00:36:12,630 --> 00:36:14,320
It's to treat everyone
with absolute equality.

931
00:36:14,320 --> 00:36:15,400
The most important thing for a cadre

932
00:36:15,400 --> 00:36:16,300
is to be fair and impartial,

933
00:36:16,300 --> 00:36:17,500
not to treat everyone
with absolute equality.

934
00:36:17,500 --> 00:36:18,690
If you don't treat everyone
with absolute equality...

935
00:36:18,690 --> 00:36:19,770
How could they be the same?

936
00:36:19,770 --> 00:36:20,270
How are they different?

937
00:36:20,270 --> 00:36:21,130
If you don't...

938
00:36:21,150 --> 00:36:21,840
Indeed.

939
00:36:21,840 --> 00:36:22,970
Village Secretary.

940
00:36:23,280 --> 00:36:24,230
Gaoyuan didn't say

941
00:36:24,230 --> 00:36:25,830
anything offensive, did he?

942
00:36:26,230 --> 00:36:27,030
No, he didn't.

943
00:36:27,590 --> 00:36:28,300
We were just talking about

944
00:36:28,300 --> 00:36:30,030
your teaching qualification.

945
00:36:30,280 --> 00:36:31,440
Aren't you going to swap the land?

946
00:36:31,440 --> 00:36:31,840
Accountant,

947
00:36:31,840 --> 00:36:33,590
help them swap the land tomorrow.

948
00:36:33,590 --> 00:36:34,800
No need. It's really not necessary.

949
00:36:34,800 --> 00:36:36,150
I beg you. No need.

950
00:36:36,170 --> 00:36:37,230
Okay? Listen to me.

951
00:36:59,360 --> 00:36:59,920
What?

952
00:37:02,320 --> 00:37:02,730
Gaoyuan.

953
00:37:02,730 --> 00:37:03,760
Calm down.

954
00:37:03,920 --> 00:37:04,630
You can't go.

955
00:37:04,630 --> 00:37:06,180
You can't go. Calm down.

956
00:37:06,280 --> 00:37:07,340
-What?
-Calm down.

957
00:37:16,280 --> 00:37:17,080
Chen Yizhong.

958
00:37:17,510 --> 00:37:17,810
Hey,

959
00:37:17,830 --> 00:37:19,300
are you addicted to this?

960
00:37:19,650 --> 00:37:21,280
Are you going to
ask bluntly just like that?

961
00:37:21,280 --> 00:37:22,670
What could you possibly find out?

962
00:37:22,670 --> 00:37:24,110
If you don't ask,
won't it be harder for you to find out?

963
00:37:24,110 --> 00:37:24,850
Exactly.

964
00:37:24,880 --> 00:37:26,150
It won't hurt to ask.

965
00:37:26,360 --> 00:37:27,400
Didn't you guys get the testimony

966
00:37:27,400 --> 00:37:28,800
from Liu Erlin by asking?

967
00:37:29,660 --> 00:37:30,840
How could that be the same?

968
00:37:30,840 --> 00:37:32,560
Qiu Agui's case
is about killing her husband.

969
00:37:32,560 --> 00:37:33,710
It's only been a few days,

970
00:37:33,710 --> 00:37:36,640
and my legs have gotten thicker
from all this riding.

971
00:37:37,280 --> 00:37:38,150
Besides,

972
00:37:38,150 --> 00:37:39,190
why can't you two

973
00:37:39,190 --> 00:37:40,230
ride your own bikes?

974
00:37:40,230 --> 00:37:41,360
Why do you need others to give you a ride?

975
00:37:41,360 --> 00:37:42,320
As a grown man,

976
00:37:42,320 --> 00:37:44,110
you should contribute your strength.

977
00:37:44,110 --> 00:37:44,510
Lihui!

978
00:37:44,880 --> 00:37:45,680
Get on my bike!

979
00:37:45,930 --> 00:37:47,530
I have something to tell you.

980
00:37:51,230 --> 00:37:52,830
You're not as heavy as she is.

981
00:37:53,320 --> 00:37:53,720
You...

982
00:37:55,070 --> 00:37:56,550
-Get on the bike.
-Let's go.

983
00:37:56,550 --> 00:37:57,610
Cushion your butt.

984
00:38:01,070 --> 00:38:01,600
Let's go.

985
00:38:05,360 --> 00:38:05,890
Let's go!

986
00:38:22,510 --> 00:38:24,040
How about I ride for a while?

987
00:38:30,480 --> 00:38:30,840
Hya!

988
00:38:32,190 --> 00:38:32,550
Hya!

989
00:38:33,360 --> 00:38:33,800
What?

990
00:38:34,190 --> 00:38:34,550
Hya!

991
00:38:35,150 --> 00:38:35,630
Go!

992
00:38:36,510 --> 00:38:36,920
Hurry!

993
00:38:45,260 --> 00:38:45,720
Get out!

994
00:38:46,110 --> 00:38:46,550
Get out!

995
00:38:46,550 --> 00:38:47,110
Ma'am! Ma'am!

996
00:38:47,110 --> 00:38:47,570
Get out!

997
00:38:48,540 --> 00:38:49,510
If you don't get out now,

998
00:38:49,510 --> 00:38:50,500
I'll call for help!

999
00:38:50,500 --> 00:38:51,760
Don't be angry, Ma'am.

1000
00:38:52,630 --> 00:38:54,360
My son died such a tragic death,

1001
00:38:54,760 --> 00:38:57,150
but you're
still speaking for the murderer.

1002
00:38:57,150 --> 00:38:58,040
Get out!

1003
00:38:58,230 --> 00:39:00,030
All of you, get out!

1004
00:39:00,480 --> 00:39:02,340
W-We're not speaking for anyone.

1005
00:39:02,400 --> 00:39:03,230
We want to know the truth.

1006
00:39:03,230 --> 00:39:03,590
Ma'am!

1007
00:39:03,590 --> 00:39:04,390
Ma'am! Ma'am!

1008
00:39:05,320 --> 00:39:05,760
Ma'am!

1009
00:39:19,030 --> 00:39:19,760
Are you okay?

1010
00:39:23,630 --> 00:39:25,670
What is this and why is it so smelly?

1011
00:39:31,510 --> 00:39:32,170
Pig manure.

1012
00:39:32,550 --> 00:39:34,010
Just... Just stand there.

1013
00:39:34,230 --> 00:39:34,950
Don't move.

1014
00:39:38,230 --> 00:39:38,760
I'm dirty.

1015
00:39:38,760 --> 00:39:39,570
Don't come near me!

1016
00:39:39,570 --> 00:39:40,550
Don't come near me!

1017
00:39:40,550 --> 00:39:41,610
Don't come near me!

1018
00:39:48,150 --> 00:39:49,320
Like mother,

1019
00:39:49,320 --> 00:39:50,360
like son.

1020
00:39:52,880 --> 00:39:54,510
If you were her,
in terms of your personality,

1021
00:39:54,510 --> 00:39:56,310
you might have poured acid on us.

1022
00:39:56,440 --> 00:39:57,840
You have a good personality.

1023
00:39:57,840 --> 00:39:58,710
You're tough.

1024
00:40:02,480 --> 00:40:04,070
I don't think it's useful to ask her.

1025
00:40:04,070 --> 00:40:04,670
Why?

1026
00:40:05,230 --> 00:40:05,880
In the countryside,

1027
00:40:05,880 --> 00:40:08,320
blood ties are more important
than anything else.

1028
00:40:08,320 --> 00:40:10,320
If you don't believe me, go ask them.

1029
00:40:11,840 --> 00:40:13,300
Alright. I'll go ask them.

1030
00:40:13,510 --> 00:40:14,320
You... Stop.

1031
00:40:15,070 --> 00:40:15,880
It's not clean yet.

1032
00:40:15,880 --> 00:40:16,810
Lower your head.

1033
00:40:16,920 --> 00:40:18,110
Just take a break.

1034
00:40:18,630 --> 00:40:19,280
The smell on you

1035
00:40:19,280 --> 00:40:20,680
will scare them all away.

1036
00:40:21,480 --> 00:40:22,140
Let me do it.

1037
00:40:26,190 --> 00:40:26,760
Ma'am!

1038
00:40:29,070 --> 00:40:30,230
Hello, we...

1039
00:40:30,710 --> 00:40:32,280
We... We are not bad people.

1040
00:40:40,510 --> 00:40:41,880
Here you are. Wipe your hair.

1041
00:40:41,880 --> 00:40:42,740
Wipe your hair.

1042
00:40:43,930 --> 00:40:45,930
Hello, we are from the county court.

1043
00:40:46,000 --> 00:40:46,710
We want to learn about

1044
00:40:46,710 --> 00:40:49,110
the situation of Huang Liancang's family.

1045
00:40:49,360 --> 00:40:49,890
Alright.

1046
00:40:50,970 --> 00:40:51,840
I think the people in this village

1047
00:40:51,840 --> 00:40:52,640
are hopeless.

1048
00:40:54,080 --> 00:40:55,330
To them,

1049
00:40:55,360 --> 00:40:56,690
Qiu Agui is an outsider.

1050
00:40:56,960 --> 00:40:57,560
Outsider?

1051
00:40:58,000 --> 00:40:58,460
Well...

1052
00:40:58,720 --> 00:40:59,590
Didn't they all marry into this village

1053
00:40:59,590 --> 00:41:00,650
from other places?

1054
00:41:01,150 --> 00:41:02,210
That's different.

1055
00:41:03,710 --> 00:41:05,310
Well, what Lihui means is...

1056
00:41:06,440 --> 00:41:07,400
what Qiu Agui did this time

1057
00:41:07,400 --> 00:41:08,530
wasn't just murder.

1058
00:41:08,850 --> 00:41:10,080
This time, she hurt

1059
00:41:10,110 --> 00:41:12,360
the entire village's pride and feelings.

1060
00:41:12,360 --> 00:41:13,030
Her husband beating her

1061
00:41:13,030 --> 00:41:14,290
was their own family business.

1062
00:41:14,290 --> 00:41:15,400
Now that she has killed him
just for beating her,

1063
00:41:15,400 --> 00:41:16,250
how can other families

1064
00:41:16,250 --> 00:41:17,150
enforce their family rules in the future?

1065
00:41:17,150 --> 00:41:17,550
Right?

1066
00:41:18,590 --> 00:41:19,790
Being tied down here,

1067
00:41:20,110 --> 00:41:21,710
they can't bear it or escape.

1068
00:41:22,030 --> 00:41:23,480
Then they often go to extremes

1069
00:41:23,480 --> 00:41:24,810
or even commit suicide.

1070
00:41:24,960 --> 00:41:26,290
Previously, I heard

1071
00:41:26,320 --> 00:41:27,710
the sociology department say that

1072
00:41:27,710 --> 00:41:28,760
the suicide rate among rural women

1073
00:41:28,760 --> 00:41:29,520
was alarmingly high.

1074
00:41:29,520 --> 00:41:31,120
The figures would shock you.

1075
00:41:31,760 --> 00:41:33,020
So we came here in vain?

1076
00:41:34,030 --> 00:41:35,230
I refuse to accept it!

1077
00:41:35,510 --> 00:41:37,150
Will it help if you refuse to accept it?

1078
00:41:37,150 --> 00:41:39,030
Even if you find something out,

1079
00:41:39,190 --> 00:41:40,800
would they
provide their testimonies for you?

1080
00:41:40,800 --> 00:41:41,800
How would they continue to

1081
00:41:41,800 --> 00:41:42,760
stay in this village after that?

1082
00:41:42,760 --> 00:41:43,960
So we're just going to watch her

1083
00:41:43,960 --> 00:41:44,480
get sentenced to death

1084
00:41:44,480 --> 00:41:45,610
and do nothing, huh?

1085
00:41:46,320 --> 00:41:48,320
Let me say something you won't like.

1086
00:41:49,110 --> 00:41:50,670
We're running around here
like headless chickens,

1087
00:41:50,670 --> 00:41:51,670
and that's more about

1088
00:41:51,670 --> 00:41:53,000
satisfying ourselves.

1089
00:41:53,440 --> 00:41:54,970
Why do you have to be so mean?

1090
00:41:55,070 --> 00:41:56,600
How am I satisfying myself?

1091
00:41:57,360 --> 00:41:59,110
A helpless sense of justice.

1092
00:41:59,550 --> 00:42:01,630
I'm talking about not just you

1093
00:42:01,920 --> 00:42:02,850
but also myself.

1094
00:42:03,280 --> 00:42:04,850
I'm not like Yu Gaoyuan,

1095
00:42:04,880 --> 00:42:05,590
who always excludes himself

1096
00:42:05,590 --> 00:42:06,480
before criticizing others.

1097
00:42:06,480 --> 00:42:07,930
I'm better at self-criticism.

1098
00:42:07,930 --> 00:42:09,440
When you're talking, your mouth...

1099
00:42:09,440 --> 00:42:10,730
You're really annoying.

1100
00:42:10,730 --> 00:42:11,630
Let me tell you. You're always like that.

1101
00:42:11,630 --> 00:42:13,030
Y-You can give her a ride.

1102
00:42:13,030 --> 00:42:13,630
Take care of her.

1103
00:42:13,630 --> 00:42:14,840
I have to get this straight with you.

1104
00:42:14,840 --> 00:42:16,340
How am I satisfying myself?

1105
00:42:16,340 --> 00:42:17,630
How am I satisfying myself?

1106
00:42:17,630 --> 00:42:18,230
I'm not...

1107
00:42:18,280 --> 00:42:19,190
Slow down!

1108
00:42:25,550 --> 00:42:26,750
What should we do now?

1109
00:42:28,030 --> 00:42:28,630
Comrades.

1110
00:42:29,630 --> 00:42:30,480
If we miss this chance,

1111
00:42:30,480 --> 00:42:32,010
there won't be another one.

1112
00:42:33,280 --> 00:42:33,880
Comrades.

1113
00:42:34,960 --> 00:42:36,840
A-Are you from the court?

1114
00:42:37,550 --> 00:42:37,920
Yes.

1115
00:42:38,280 --> 00:42:40,070
We are all from the county court.

1116
00:42:40,070 --> 00:42:41,330
My name is Xia Yingjie.

1117
00:42:42,000 --> 00:42:43,730
Are you also from this village?

1118
00:42:45,480 --> 00:42:46,190
Sort of.

1119
00:42:47,030 --> 00:42:47,960
But not exactly.

1120
00:42:49,070 --> 00:42:51,270
Qiu Agui and I are from the same village.

1121
00:42:51,320 --> 00:42:53,250
We married into this one together.

1122
00:42:55,000 --> 00:42:55,800
Just like her,

1123
00:42:56,400 --> 00:42:58,400
I get beaten by my husband every day.

1124
00:42:58,710 --> 00:43:00,030
My husband's name is Feng Dazhi.
